    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2c9f53be_77b17a3b",
        "filename": "microdroid/signature/signature.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-14T14:30:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027d like to keep this for clarity.",
      "parentUuid": "7a3d0012_f5321eea",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "5b570314f3140baf7d21ad3167c1c663753ed199",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "155dd4fa_4716bb82",
        "filename": "microdroid/signature/signature.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-14T23:21:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this rather adds confusion with no benefit. Endianness is not important here.",
      "parentUuid": "2c9f53be_77b17a3b",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "5b570314f3140baf7d21ad3167c1c663753ed199",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "4699fe96_a6bb1efb",
        "filename": "microdroid/signature/signature.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T00:03:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Endianness is important when you read/write a number to/from a file. A file can be generated in another machine and downloaded/pushed. Yeah this may not be the typical case (just for debugging?), but I don\u0027t see any strong reason to move away from the possibility.",
      "parentUuid": "155dd4fa_4716bb82",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "5b570314f3140baf7d21ad3167c1c663753ed199",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "82b3b55a_efd94c9c",
        "filename": "microdroid/signature/signature.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1132673
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T00:18:25Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t expect this file will be generated in another machine; out design doesn\u0027t have the case. Even if we have the case perhaps for debugging, arm/x86 are both LE, so no need to care about endianness in practice.",
      "parentUuid": "4699fe96_a6bb1efb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "5b570314f3140baf7d21ad3167c1c663753ed199",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "319cc927_9b1c0f1d",
        "filename": "microdroid/signature/signature.cc",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 41,
      "author": {
        "id": 1415877
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-04-15T00:23:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Even in that case, I\u0027d like to be specific about endianness (so changing it to LE instead BE). It eliminates the need to know all about it: what machine types do we support (as of now, or in the near future) and these files can\u0027t be generated from other machine and ... \n\nWhy not simply saying \u00274byte unsigned integer in BE(or LE, if you want to avoid byteswaps for practicality)\u0027?",
      "parentUuid": "82b3b55a_efd94c9c",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 41,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 41,
        "endChar": 18
      },
      "revId": "5b570314f3140baf7d21ad3167c1c663753ed199",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
